AREA 10: CONFIDENCE TERMINOLOGY & CALIBRATION DISTINCTION
======================================================================
  Distinction between Decision Confidence vs Statistical Probability Calibration:
  1. Predicted-Class Decision Confidence: Confidence = P(ASD) for ASD; 1 - P(ASD) for Control.
     This strictly defines how confident the model is in its chosen classification relative to tau=0.50.
  2. Statistical Calibration: Statistical calibration across empirical probability bins is
     evidenced by the Test-Set Brier score of 0.041963 (~0.0420).
     Individual single-patient predictions are decision confidences, not post-hoc Platt calibrated probabilities.
  -> Confidence Terminology: PASS

